Basic usage<pre><code>from ttl_cache import ttl_lru_cache


@ttl_lru_cache(ttl=30)  # (1)!
def fetch_user(user_id: int) -&gt; dict:
    print("Fetching from the network...")
    return {"id": user_id, "name": "Ada"}


fetch_user(1)  # Prints "Fetching from the network..."
fetch_user(1)  # Cache hit, nothing printed
# ... 30 seconds later ...
fetch_user(1)  # Expired — fetches again
</code></pre> <ol> <li>Cache results for 30 seconds. While the TTL window is open, repeat calls     with the same arguments are served from the cache.</li> </ol>
